WEBVTT

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.720
Arusu was caught in an explosion
at the Interdimensional Sea...

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.519
...and went missing along with Lennon.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:03.028
With Arusu gone, both Eva and
Sheila finally understood...

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.895
...that having her around
was very important.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.199
But then, Arusu came back to the
Magical Realm all of a sudden.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.068
How did she come back?

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.066
On the other hand,
the True Book of Spells...

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.872
...was in Lennon's possession.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.801
Tweeny Witches

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:59.801
Suspicion

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:05.517
When I was little, Yoko used
to read me a bedtime story.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.179
"Through the Looking Glass,
and What Alice Found There."

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:13.190
There's another world on the
other side of the mirror, and a girl...

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:16.422
...named Alice gets
sucked into that world.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.828
Ouch...

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.097
You want that mirror?

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:22.828
What?

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.834
Oh, hi...

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:29.836
Who was the person that
lured Alice into the mirror?

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.111
What? No way!

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.577
Bucky is going to sleep with Arusu?

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.082
But we don't have enough rooms.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:40.084
| mean, what's with the name?
What's Bucky?

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.952
A pirate is also known
as a buccaneer, right?

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.921
That's why it's Bucky!

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:49.086
No, the pirate Lennon!

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.558
Don't bring any weird objects in here.
This place isn't that big.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:55.657
You should check what you're
wearing before you head out.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.430
That's a common practice
for a lady, Sheila.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.801
Yeah, right. What lady?

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.969
Did you say something?

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:03.907
Oh, nothing.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.105
You said something! You said
something about me being a lady...

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.977
Stop fighting!

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.014
Right.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:16.252
Bucky's resting comfortably.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:20.326
What about a good night?
You didn't say good night.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.589
Are you heading out again?

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:30.592
Stay here. Don't let the pirate
leave with that True Book of Spells.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.471
Great.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:41.846
As long as you have that light of hope,
you can do anything, little girl.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.582
You can do anything...

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.880
Eva is amazing!

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:56.054
Apprentice witch.
Which district are you from?

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.658
Answer me!

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.264
What?

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.360
How come your hair is short?

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:08.064
Pancakes or hotcakes.
Which do you like better?

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.972
| don't really care.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.808
Why do you have the True Book of Spells?

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:17.076
This book suddenly appeared before me.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.684
All of a sudden one day.

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.776
| guess the ecoo did it.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.446
But why did it appear before you?

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.355
I told you before.
Because we're mirrors.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:27.503
You and I.

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:29.723
You and I.
Mirrors, eh? Then what?

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:34.857
You reached out from the mirror and took
the book or pulled me from the mirror...

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:38.164
| was always alone. I wandered
around the Interdimensional Sea...

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.669
...all by myself.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.833
You're lying. I've never heard of
that kind of an apprentice witch.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.068
I'm not lying.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:48.008
You probably couldn't use any magic,
so they sent you to the Human Realm.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:51.175
And you've been wandering
around the Interdimensional Sea.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:56.019
Maybe you're thinking of getting back
at those witches who sent you away.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:58.852
If that's what you think,
then you don't need to ask.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:05:59.535
You...

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.550
You...
Take it easy now, Sheila.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:03.493
Come on, let's not fight.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.868
Let's see...

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:11.661
This is it.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:15.808
A list of all apprentice witches
who were sent to the Human Realm.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.208
Lennon...

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.211
Lennon...

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.471
It's not in here. Why?

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:24.215
Lennon is not an apprentice witch?

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.145
Yeah.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:28.284
She's not listed in the
registry of apprentice witches...

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:31.483
...nor the list of apprentice witches
who were sent to the Human Realm.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:35.050
Well, I'm not on the list either.
Besides, I'm a human...

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:38.559
Wait, so you're telling me
that Lennon is a human?

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:40.560
Any idea?

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.363
It seems that we're
mirrors of each other...

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.369
But why did you look that up?

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.564
Well...

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.283
Bucky's not human.

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.103
Bucky's not human.
Huh!

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:53.377
Come on. You should tell us that
you're listening to our conversation.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.471
Can you stop snooping around like that?

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:57.612
What?

00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:02.017
If you want to know something,
then ask me in person.

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:06.349
| don't know, Lennon.
The way you talk is...

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:08.826
I thought I told you that I'm a pirate.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.397
What else do you want to know about me?

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:15.924
No, it's just that this thing
about the mirror is kind of...

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:18.732
Forget it. Let's go out on patrol!

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:23.269
Sheila is acting strange.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:26.471
She's awfully harsh towards Bucky.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.104
What are you doing?

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:34.115
Don't the names Arusu and Alice...

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:36.077
...sound alike?

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:37.212
Alice?

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.654
Alice who was lured to the
other side of the mirror...

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:42.057
...and was asked by the queen
to play a game of chess.

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:45.290
Alice was the one who got the checkmate.
And they lived happily ever after.

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:46.490
What is that?

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:51.069
Alice. Who asked you to go to
the other side of the mirror?

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:54.138
Man, did Yoko really
read the story correctly?

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.334
| can't remember it at all.

00:07:56.876 --> 00:08:00.369
Not you too, Arusu.
What is wrong with you two?

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.777
They're here!

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:11.383
Can't you understand that
we're telling you to let them go free?

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:14.017
They won't listen to anything we say.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:18.124
You're not going anywhere!

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:19.287
Oh no!

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:23.601
Supplement, analog, struggle!

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:28.333
You did great, Eva!

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:30.308
This way!

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:34.171
Find them!

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:37.951
Hey, fairies. Hang in there
just a bit longer, okay?

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.795
What's the point of doing this?

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.913
What's the point of doing this?
| don't think you know about this...

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:45.855
...but we're the Magical Girl Squad.
We fight for justice.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:49.394
Our first priority is to live in
symbiosis with the fairies and...

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:52.465
...find a way to attain
sources of magic.

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:55.364
| don't know about those
complicated things, but...

00:08:55.468 --> 00:08:58.631
We're trying to protect the
fairies from being captured.

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.729
But this realm will be destroyed, right?

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.502
Spending your remaining
moments protecting fairies.

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:04.520
Aren't you going to regret it?

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:07.172
Aren't you going to regret it?
You really don't get it, Lennon.

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:09.475
We don't have much time left...

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:13.075
...50 that's why we're doing
our best to protect magic.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:16.579
Then there will be no destruction.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.885
Because magic creates miracles.

00:09:20.126 --> 00:09:23.096
Magic makes everyone happy.

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:25.821
You just said a great thing, Arusu!

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:27.955
Say that again.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:28.761
Nope.

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:29.960
Meanie.

00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:31.934
Then what do you want to do?

00:09:32.038 --> 00:09:35.406
You have better things to do
with the time you're left with?

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:38.744
There they are!

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.642
Just as I suspected...

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.741
I'll draw their attention!

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.246
Hey! I'm over here!

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:46.361
Fairies are over here!

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:49.184
Fairies are over here!
If this is the witch who uses dark magic...

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:51.414
...then the warlocks won't attack.

00:09:51.524 --> 00:09:53.288
Hold on to them for me.

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:53.969
Let's go, Eva!

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:55.188
Let's go, Eva!
What? But...

00:09:55.394 --> 00:10:00.093
Even attacked, the pirate would
fight back with dark magic...

00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:00.922
Hey!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.729
| found the fairies!

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.828
Lennon!

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:06.899
Hold it!

00:10:06.973 --> 00:10:08.964
What are you saying, Sheila?

00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:12.238
This is a good chance to
find out who that really is.

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:13.589
You want to find out too, don't you?

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:15.308
You want to find out too, don't you?
Yeah, but...

00:10:15.581 --> 00:10:16.309
Fire!

00:10:19.785 --> 00:10:21.310
Bucky! Fly!

00:10:21.454 --> 00:10:24.913
But if Lennon dies,
then we'll never find out!

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:30.120
Mountain hut, high leg, rock 'n' roll.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.532
Damn! Retreat! Go back!

00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:45.743
It's just not right, Sheila.
Doing things like that.

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:49.639
| can't tell you now, but it's
for the future of this realm.

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:52.743
Bucky. You can't use any magic?

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:55.114
Then I can teach you how.

00:10:55.221 --> 00:10:59.124
| wish magic would disappear
from this realm for good.

00:10:59.558 --> 00:11:00.423
Lennon?

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.324
You said magic is supposed
to make everyone happy, right?

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:06.829
Then I'll tell you one thing.

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:08.827
Even if there's magic...

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:12.393
...there are witches that can
only bring misfortune to others.

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:15.736
| don't remember who
called her out there...

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:18.071
But I do remember one thing for sure.

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:21.078
Alice went to the land on the
other side of the mirror...

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.946
...and it was definitely the exact
opposite. Like a mirror image.

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:36.317
Tweeny Witches

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:45.326
Splintered Hearts

00:11:48.007 --> 00:11:50.135
Why? That was mine...

00:11:50.242 --> 00:11:55.009
You said you wished that magic
would disappear from this realm.

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:58.549
No, you were probably
just hearing things.

00:11:58.651 --> 00:12:01.450
You just want the magic to disappear?

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:04.046
Or is there something else?

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:05.751
Magic.

00:12:07.159 --> 00:12:08.217
That's why.

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:10.962
You'll be held responsible.

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:19.566
Every single day,
| eat this same, awful food!

00:12:19.672 --> 00:12:21.299
| can't eat this anymore!

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.134
Eat it.

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:27.246
If you stay alive, then there's a
chance for us to get out one day.

00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:29.541
How long were you in here?

00:12:29.749 --> 00:12:30.910
Let's see...

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:33.880
It's probably been six years...

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.815
Let go! Let me go!

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:37.411
| said let me go!

00:12:37.623 --> 00:12:40.251
| don't want to fly! I hate magic!

00:12:40.359 --> 00:12:41.002
Get me down!

00:12:41.026 --> 00:12:41.857
Get me down!
Okay.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:46.287
Just kidding.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:48.059
What are they doing?

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:51.933
She's trying to teach Bucky
that magic is the greatest.

00:12:52.037 --> 00:12:54.369
Jeez. She has no sense of urgency.

00:12:54.807 --> 00:12:56.468
Where did you go?

00:12:56.742 --> 00:12:59.439
Not just yesterday,
but every single night.

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:00.306
Don't ask.

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:02.904
You usually ask things like this!
I'm worried!

00:13:03.015 --> 00:13:04.107
Please don't.

00:13:05.151 --> 00:13:07.984
If that's not the one, then...

00:13:10.256 --> 00:13:12.657
Yes, I don't mind.

00:13:13.025 --> 00:13:15.323
| have no regrets.

00:13:15.427 --> 00:13:17.794
Credelle? Is something wrong?

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.592
| heard a very loud noise in there.

00:13:20.699 --> 00:13:22.167
It's nothing.

00:13:22.601 --> 00:13:24.569
Don't come in. Go away.

00:13:24.904 --> 00:13:25.996
Okay.

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:30.707
Of course, I'll need to
be compensated handsomely.

00:13:31.076 --> 00:13:33.807
Yes. Then I'll see you on
the night of the red moon.

00:13:34.013 --> 00:13:35.572
Where's Sheila?

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:39.675
She's been going out for the
past couple of nights, and...

00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:42.078
...she never tells me anything.

00:13:42.521 --> 00:13:43.920
Where's Sheila?

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:47.387
She came back, but
she won't come out of her room.

00:13:47.459 --> 00:13:48.449
| see.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:51.924
There!

00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:53.427
Ta-da!

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:58.333
You wanna know how I did it?
It's magic.

00:13:59.305 --> 00:14:01.034
| don't care about magic...

00:14:01.106 --> 00:14:04.565
Oh, don't give me that.
You really like magic, don't you?

00:14:05.744 --> 00:14:07.906
You're all paying attention to Bucky!

00:14:08.013 --> 00:14:10.277
Are you even listening to me?

00:14:10.382 --> 00:14:11.713
What?

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:15.450
Are you a human?

00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:16.453
Yeah...

00:14:16.889 --> 00:14:20.189
I'm surprised.
I've never seen a male human before.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:21.893
Why are you here?

00:14:21.961 --> 00:14:23.827
| came here to look for my son.

00:14:23.929 --> 00:14:24.555
Your son?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.256
Yeah.

00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:30.262
We were separated on the
Interdimensional Sea 13 years ago.

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:31.996
You're a weird guy.

00:14:32.137 --> 00:14:35.630
What is a human like yourself doing
here and on the Interdimensional Sea?

00:14:35.741 --> 00:14:37.800
Plus you even had a son...

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.377
Son?

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:41.677
You know something?

00:14:41.981 --> 00:14:44.882
No, but that's not it...

00:14:45.951 --> 00:14:48.477
Fine! I can use my magic now.

00:14:48.621 --> 00:14:52.683
I'll learn lots of spells and
protect the fairies on my own!

00:14:53.225 --> 00:14:55.193
Quake spell?

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:57.190
This is an attack spell?

00:14:57.496 --> 00:14:59.555
Beard from a pan yon fairy...

00:14:59.732 --> 00:15:01.325
Maybe I can do it!

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:02.462
A girl?

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:06.428
So you're telling me that
a human girl is in this realm?

00:15:06.538 --> 00:15:09.564
Yeah. I don't know
if she's still here or not, but...

00:15:10.409 --> 00:15:13.936
You were here for six years,
but you probably don't know this.

00:15:14.046 --> 00:15:14.877
What is it?

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:18.610
This realm is going
to be destroyed soon.

00:15:19.318 --> 00:15:20.046
What?

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.584
I found you, pan yon!

00:15:26.692 --> 00:15:28.592
Let me have your beard!

00:15:34.033 --> 00:15:35.194
Eva's
gone?

00:15:35.467 --> 00:15:37.458
Yeah, she left.

00:15:37.736 --> 00:15:39.704
She said she'll protect the fairies.

00:15:39.805 --> 00:15:42.035
Why did she go by herself?

00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:45.475
We have to hurry! We gotta
get there before it's too late!

00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:50.405
You'd better let the
pan yon fairy go or else...

00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:55.883
Three of them might be hard to deal with,
but she's no match for us by herself.

00:15:55.988 --> 00:15:57.456
Making fun of me?

00:15:57.556 --> 00:16:00.753
I... Even I can use magic too, you know!

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.250
Take that!

00:16:06.398 --> 00:16:07.331
Pan yon!

00:16:09.201 --> 00:16:11.397
What should I do?

00:16:12.638 --> 00:16:15.403
If the beard is burned,
then there's no use for this thing.

00:16:15.507 --> 00:16:16.484
Okay! Let's go!

00:16:16.508 --> 00:16:17.202
Okay! Let's go!
Yeah.

00:16:18.444 --> 00:16:19.912
Water. Water...

00:16:20.045 --> 00:16:20.807
There!

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:25.126
Eva!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.015
Eva!
Eva!

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:30.918
There you go.

00:16:31.457 --> 00:16:32.424
Bye-bye!

00:16:33.425 --> 00:16:34.636
You were reckless!

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.492
You were reckless!
But the pan yon was...

00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:39.565
It was reckless for you
to go on patrol by yourself!

00:16:40.099 --> 00:16:41.999
But, Sheila, even you...

00:16:42.134 --> 00:16:42.965
What?

00:16:43.268 --> 00:16:46.533
You sneak out every night by yourself...

00:16:46.705 --> 00:16:50.039
...and Arusu is like,
"Bucky this, Bucky that!"

00:16:50.242 --> 00:16:52.734
So I decided to do things on my own.

00:16:56.115 --> 00:16:57.014
Sheila?

00:16:57.249 --> 00:17:00.651
Eva! I'm worried about Lennon,
so let's go back.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:08.358
Fine! I can use magic too!

00:17:11.263 --> 00:17:13.129
The Warlock Realm lies ahead.

00:17:13.232 --> 00:17:16.600
So she is the one who is
capable of using dark magic.

00:17:18.804 --> 00:17:21.136
We don't know why it will be destroyed.

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:24.437
But they can do nothing
to prevent it now.

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:26.942
Grande said he will seek a new world.

00:17:27.046 --> 00:17:30.448
In order to do that, he needs
the power of a special magic.

00:17:30.883 --> 00:17:32.248
Dark magic?

00:17:32.451 --> 00:17:35.682
Grande is trying to use dark magic?

00:17:35.954 --> 00:17:36.682
Yeah.

00:17:36.989 --> 00:17:39.754
He's eagerly capturing
the fairies right now.

00:17:39.892 --> 00:17:43.089
But how come you know about dark magic?

00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:44.992
This place is...

00:17:46.131 --> 00:17:47.656
| was surprised.

00:17:47.866 --> 00:17:51.598
| never expected you to go
to the Human Realm, Credelle.

00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:53.970
Is there a special reason?

00:17:54.039 --> 00:17:56.235
You promised not to ask anything.

00:17:56.308 --> 00:17:57.639
Human Realm?

00:17:57.743 --> 00:18:01.111
Does she know that this realm
is going to be destroyed?

00:18:01.213 --> 00:18:03.181
Are you fleeing all by yourself?

00:18:04.183 --> 00:18:07.118
You! What are you saying?

00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:09.812
You're supposed to be
one of the Three Sages!

00:18:09.888 --> 00:18:14.382
Don't you have any pride as a witch?
Don't you care for your friends?

00:18:14.526 --> 00:18:16.255
What about your loyalty?

00:18:16.361 --> 00:18:18.728
Don't you feel the same way I do?

00:18:18.831 --> 00:18:19.354
What?

00:18:19.965 --> 00:18:24.368
Instead of waiting for my power to
disappear and collapse like the rest...

00:18:24.603 --> 00:18:27.971
...by throwing away
both my magic and pride...

00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:32.044
I would like to live longer in the
Human Realm. That kind of feeling.

00:18:32.144 --> 00:18:34.408
Don't you feel that way at all?

00:18:34.546 --> 00:18:35.775
That's...

00:18:37.015 --> 00:18:39.143
But... But you are...

00:18:41.987 --> 00:18:46.151
I'm sure everyone wants to.
It's just that nobody knows about it.

00:18:46.325 --> 00:18:49.784
But if they all find out, then
I'm sure they'll feel the same way!

00:18:50.295 --> 00:18:51.319
Me too!

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:53.396
Both myself and Eva!

00:18:53.866 --> 00:18:56.426
If the Curse of Eternal Youth
can be removed from us...

00:18:56.502 --> 00:18:58.436
That's what we really want to do!

00:18:58.537 --> 00:19:00.471
That's what I want to do for her!

00:19:02.841 --> 00:19:04.036
Credelle?

00:19:04.143 --> 00:19:05.941
Is everything okay?

00:19:11.016 --> 00:19:13.883
The True Book of Spells
is in the Human Realm.

00:19:14.186 --> 00:19:15.813
I took it there.

00:19:15.921 --> 00:19:18.481
In order to prevent
dark magic from being used...

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:21.025
| needed to place it
where they can't get it.

00:19:21.727 --> 00:19:23.718
You're kidding. But I...

00:19:23.962 --> 00:19:25.157
| see.

00:19:25.998 --> 00:19:27.591
Now I get it.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.267
The True Book of Spells
is somewhere in this realm.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.201
What?

00:19:32.471 --> 00:19:33.666
That girl.

00:19:33.772 --> 00:19:37.902
That human girl that I met before
had the book in this realm.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.700
Could it be?

00:19:39.912 --> 00:19:42.904
This human girl that you speak of...
It can't be...

00:19:44.383 --> 00:19:46.249
Hey. Take it.

00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:59.054
I knew it. You lied to me
when you said you hate magic.

00:19:59.498 --> 00:20:03.594
| mean if you had, then you
wouldn't be treasuring that book.

00:20:03.869 --> 00:20:04.563
Arusu...

00:20:06.038 --> 00:20:07.597
Am I right?

00:20:08.006 --> 00:20:10.998
Her name is Arusu...

00:20:17.716 --> 00:20:25.680
Come on, let's go!
Without closing our eyes...

00:20:25.857 --> 00:20:33.857
Our singing and laughter
fill the vast sky.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:43.100
We're headed for
our greatest longings.

00:20:44.309 --> 00:20:49.873
There's no wish
that can't come true.

00:20:49.982 --> 00:20:54.249
Let's just believe and fly away!

00:20:54.987 --> 00:20:59.220
No matter how hopeless it seems...
If we wish hard enough...

00:20:59.324 --> 00:21:03.921
See, it'll turn info magic.

00:21:04.129 --> 00:21:09.295
Even the tiniest dream...
If it can bring somebody joy...

00:21:09.401 --> 00:21:12.462
Let's hope it does.

00:21:14.039 --> 00:21:18.533
Hey! DuDiDuWa...
We're laughing always, lalala...

00:21:18.644 --> 00:21:21.136
Let's sing your song and
smile and laugh with me.

00:21:21.246 --> 00:21:29.246
The truth is we're all waiting...

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:36.155
...for the world of our dreams.

00:21:36.261 --> 00:21:40.459
So we might as well
Just make one of our own!
